          <h3 id="security-faqs" class="faq-group-title">
            <a href="#security-faqs">I have questions about security and our data…</a>
          </h3>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-list">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button type="button" class="faq-question-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-sec-1">
              <span>Is Sage open‑source? Can we self‑host?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div id="faq-sec-1" class="faq-answer" hidden>
              <p>Yes. Sage is open‑source with a permissive license. You can self‑host in your VPC or run on‑prem. We also provide a fully managed option with the same security model and data ownership guarantees.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button type="button" class="faq-question-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-sec-2">
              <span>How secure is Sage?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div id="faq-sec-2" class="faq-answer" hidden>
              <p>We have a <a href="https://startr.cloud/policies/security/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><u>full security write-up</u></a> available on the Startr site. Startr is the company behind Sage.</p>
              <p>We take security very seriously, and we’ve built Sage to be secure by default. We use the latest security protocols, including <strong>256-bit AES encryption</strong> for all data at rest, and <strong>TLS 1.2</strong> for all data in transit. We also use <strong>OAuth 2.0</strong> for secure authentication. Moreover, for organizations that require it, we can provide <strong>on-premises deployment</strong> options to keep data entirely within your own infrastructure.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

